Arithmetic pattern in impossible values:
  Impossible: [7, 21, 35, 39]
  Differences: [14, 14, 4]
  mod 7: [0, 0, 0, 4]
  mod 14: [7, 7, 7, 11]

Note: n=5 impossible H={7}
  n=6 impossible H includes 7, 21=3*7, 35=5*7 (multiples of 7!), plus 39
  Hypothesis: H=7 is impossible for ALL n>=5 (since n=5 argument applies)

H=7 impossibility check via OCF:
  H=7 requires 2*a1 + 4*a2 + ... = 6
  Solutions: (a1=3,a2=0,...) or (a1=1,a2=1,...)
  At n=5: both impossible (THM-338)
  At n=6: both impossible (verified by data)
  HYP-1748: H=7 is impossible for all n >= 5

