  (Inspired by Bloom-Sawin-Schildkraut-Zhelezov 2025)
=================================================================

H-spectrum sizes: n=2:|H|=1  n=3:|H|=2  n=4:|H|=3  n=5:|H|=7  n=6:|H|=19  

  n=2: |H_n|=1, |H+H|=1, |H*H|=1
    |H+H|/|H|^2 = 1.0000
    |H*H|/|H|^2 = 1.0000
    |H+H|/|H| = 1.0000  (additive doubling)
    |H*H|/|H| = 1.0000  (multiplicative doubling)

  n=3: |H_n|=2, |H+H|=3, |H*H|=3
    |H+H|/|H|^2 = 0.7500
    |H*H|/|H|^2 = 0.7500
    |H+H|/|H| = 1.5000  (additive doubling)
    |H*H|/|H| = 1.5000  (multiplicative doubling)

  n=4: |H_n|=3, |H+H|=5, |H*H|=6
    |H+H|/|H|^2 = 0.5556
    |H*H|/|H|^2 = 0.6667
    |H+H|/|H| = 1.6667  (additive doubling)
    |H*H|/|H| = 2.0000  (multiplicative doubling)

  n=5: |H_n|=7, |H+H|=15, |H*H|=25
    |H+H|/|H|^2 = 0.3061
    |H*H|/|H|^2 = 0.5102
    |H+H|/|H| = 2.1429  (additive doubling)
    |H*H|/|H| = 3.5714  (multiplicative doubling)

  n=6: |H_n|=19, |H+H|=45, |H*H|=171
    |H+H|/|H|^2 = 0.1247
    |H*H|/|H|^2 = 0.4737
    |H+H|/|H| = 2.3684  (additive doubling)
    |H*H|/|H| = 9.0000  (multiplicative doubling)

Note: If H_n satisfied sum-product, we'd expect min(|H+H|,|H*H|) >= |H|^{1.5}+

